<title>UK: Inchcape to sell Kia Automobiles France.</title>
<headline>Inchcape to sell Kia Automobiles France.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British motor vehicles retail group Inchcape Plc said on Thursday its French subsidiary Inchcape France SA will sell Kia Automobiles France SARL for a &quot;nominal&quot; consideration.</p>
<p>Inchcape said its French unit will concentrate on expanding its Mazda business in France. It imports and distributes Mazda cars and parts.  </p>
<p>Inchcape said Kia Automobile France imports and distributes Kia and Asia vehicles and parts.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale will enable Inchcape France to concentrate resources and management attention onto the Mazda business and is in line with the Inchcape group strategy of focusing on fewer businesses with scale potential,&quot; Inchcape said in a statement.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
